    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03574v1</id>
    <title>The phase diagram of the complex continuous random energy model: The weak correlation regime</title>
    <updated>2023-04-07T10:13:30Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03574v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.03574v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We identify the fluctuations of the partition function of the continuous random energy model on a Galton-Watson tree in the so-called weak correlation regime. Namely, when the ``speed functions'', that describe the time-inhomogeneous variance, lie strictly below their concave hull and satisfy a certain weak regularity condition. We prove that the phase diagram coincides with the one of the random energy model. However, the fluctuations are different and depend on the slope of the covariance function at $0$ and the final time $t$.</summary>
